,"event_uuid":"cd75f448-0703-4cd1-9b54-f08df2a4b4d5","position":{"commit_sha":"12a8e9d3aef429637e64040028ebe19e84d77aa7","position":"1785390203430273001-cd75f448-0703-4cd1-9b54-f08df2a4b4d5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"40a82ed5e4fdb7ffa58b37478712f259772d59d413a6d2dde3b18399464e499d","event_uuid":"f3ac1986-50dc-4fd4-bd11-9660fe7cd045","position":{"commit_sha":"ba48696caf27ba62ca1304b2bb10b93c48f03b51","position":"1785397177986635001-f3ac1986-50dc-4fd4-bd11-9660fe7cd045"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"5296622ecea3208c7eaaf4442ffb6b039c1c9672340d7b3b294006d547ed7433","event_uuid":"5b7bab0a-558b-484d-85b3-1d47bef41c3b","position":{"commit_sha":"ba48696caf27ba62ca1304b2bb10b93c48f03b51","position":"1785397178400541001-5b7bab0a-558b-484d-85b3-1d47bef41c3b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"9dfd265956de69756277cff6a849c8846763674f8f62ef410280cc6207cc20f6","event_uuid":"e5d6944b-d660-436d-a604-7f6d07de18ba","position":{"commit_sha":"7486e0a667f30b6ec5544818674d2a30f1586503","position":"1785397498742783574-e5d6944b-d660-436d-a604-7f6d07de18ba"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-220_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"d1ad70ed-ce91-4b63-9f32-e6b36aea17d4","comments":[],"created_at":1785384394621335001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"4378590e-6056-4d2c-b379-1d6ff9169e88","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"63fd-3465-b665-4a67"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nT11's POST-ROLLBACK SCHEMA STATE paragraph is a stock-finding generator: 8 of 21 sampled findings were near-identical \"plan does not assert post-rollback state\" advisories that are tautologies against an append-only store (median priority ~0.1), drowning its rare real catches (e.g. the 114f fold-in overwrite data-loss bug). The operator approved a constraint and rejected a per-plan cap; the constraint must be portable across stacks (no store technology named).\n\n## Approach\nReplace the post-rollback paragraph in src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_T11.md with a four-condition applicability rule: raise post-rollback-state findings ONLY when the plan (a) changes how existing persisted records are interpreted, (b) rewrites or migrates records in place, (c) removes or narrows a read path, or (d) performs a one-way transformation with no back-out. Add the explicit anti-false-positive line: purely additive, backward-compatible persistence changes that existing readers ignore (new record/event types, optional fields, new tables or columns with defaults) do not qualify — residual data after rollback is the norm in append-only and backward-compatible systems, not a risk. No store technology is named in the applicability rule itself, so it applies equally to SQL migrations, event stores, document databases, and config formats. Posture stays advisory. Alternative rejected: a one-finding-per-plan cap — operator rejected it; the applicability rule removes the tautology class at the source instead.\n\n## Scope\nsrc/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_T11.md, tests/unit/test_plan_review_t11_rubric.py (new, beside the other plan-review rubric contract tests in tests/unit/), docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md (regenerated).\n\n## Testing\nRubric text assertions in tests/unit/test_plan_review_t11_rubric.py: the four conditions and the anti-FP line are present; the old unconditional post-rollback wording is gone; the applicability rule names no store technology (the illustrative anti-FP examples are exempt from that assertion).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The rubric raises post-rollback findings only under the four named conditions (checked: `pytest tests/unit/test_plan_review_t11_rubric.py` asserting the conditions and absence of the old wording).\n- [ ] The anti-FP line for additive backward-compatible changes is present (checked: same test file).\n- [ ] The criteria guide is regenerated (checked: committed regen output).","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_T11.md","reason":"portable constraint"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_plan_review_t11_rubric.py","reason":"text assertions"},{"path":"docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md","reason":"regenerated"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","a492-3e46-ca44-40a5"],["relates_to","63fd-3465-b665-4a67"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"a492-3e46-ca44-40a5","parent_status_uuid":"f3ac1986-50dc-4fd4-bd11-9660fe7cd045","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"ef01-79fe-f287-4fec","ticket_type":"task","title":"Portable persistence-safety constraint for the T11 migration rubric","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["7515589